<title>BELGIUM: Germany still on EMU track despite jobless - Juncker.</title>
<headline>Germany still on EMU track despite jobless - Juncker.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Luxembourg Prime Minister Jean-Claude Juncker said on Monday that revisions in Germany's jobless forecast over the weekend had not changed his opinion about Germany's ability to meet economic and monetary union criteria.</p>
<p>&quot;My conviction still holds that the Germans will meet the currency criteria,&quot; he said on arrival for a European Union finance ministers meeting in Brussels.  </p>
<p>Germany on Sunday raised its unemployment forecast for 1997, punching a hole in Bonn's budget and hurting its chances of qualifying for the single European currency.</p>
<p>The Finance Ministry said the government had lifted its forecast for average unemployment this year by about 120,000 from an earlier prediction of 4.1 million.</p>
<p>But he said Germany was sticking with its estimate that gross domestic product (GDP) would rise by 2.5 percent this year.</p>
<p>-- Brussels newsroom +32-2-287-6800</p>
